Title: "What Is Checked"
Id: "8b5700cc-4d7d-480e-a424-eece3673778e"

Text: "`mlg check` validates configuration, collection structure, parsing,
identities, signatures, scope, requirements, target completeness, capabilities,
and group-specific rules. It emits errors rather than warnings.

**Configuration and collection.** `mlg.json` fields and types are checked;
`outputDir` must be a nonempty relative path inside the collection. Every
directory `toc` must list each direct child exactly once. A targeted check still
loads the whole collection.

**Parsing.** Proto line/indentation syntax, structural labels and order, and
formulation syntax report separate diagnostics. `mlg` code fences inside prose
are parsed as source; `mlg-fragment` fences are illustrative only.

**Identity and uniqueness.** Loading normally inserts a fresh UUID `Id:` into a
missing top-level item. IDs and command signatures must be unique, at most one
top-level `Writing:` item is allowed, and an operator/function key has at most
one `Disambiguates:`. Spec-infix headings belong only to `Declares:`; refined
headings belong only to `Refines:`.

**Documentation.** `Declares:`, `Defines:`, `Realizes:`, and `States:` require
`Documented:` with `called:` or `written:`. `Refines:` requires `adjective:` and
rejects `called:`.

**References and signatures.** Every command use must resolve with the declared
curly groups, tails, invocation groups, optional tails, variadic shape, and
mapping-parameter specialization. Its `when:` and inline context requirements
must be established at the use site.

**Scope.** Symbols are processed in source order. A right-hand expression,
command argument, spec target, or conclusion may use only already-known names.
A defined symbol cannot be introduced twice or shadowed by `using:`, a nested
quantifier or `let:`, another `:=`, or a `view: as:` binding. Function-form
placeholders are local; callable names are not.

**Targets.** A `Declares:` target and its components must be specified through
its relation/`via`, `extends:`, or `specifies:`. A concrete `Defines:` target
must have a known type and exactly one value for every component, through `:=`
or `expresses:`. A simple target states its type through `is` or a top-level
build; an assigned component can inherit the assigned command value's type.
`abstractly:` permits open typed components, and each
`Realizes:` item must fill all of them without adding new ones.

**Specifications and statements.** Binding positions accept `is` and ordinary
specification forms; conclusions use predicate forms such as `is?` and
`\:...?:/`. Refined declaration statements are accepted in clause binding
positions. A spec fact is valid only when the target type supplies the operator.

**Capabilities, builds, and views.** `:=>`, directed `:->`, equivalent
`:<->:`, `from:` items, `Requires: definition:`, and `Enables: view:` are
validated. A build must be justified by a fact, extension, or view. Direct
components using `..` must belong to a `Defines:` or `Realizes:` command.

**Other shapes.** Function and structural type literals, inferred arguments,
set builders, one- and two-dimensional variadics, mapping selectors, command
contexts, labels/justifications, `Equivalent:`, refinement markers, and builtin
clause commands each receive construct-specific validation."
Id: "0f8136db-1ce1-426d-b690-9ca405705e49"

SectionTitle: "Group-Specific Validations"
Id: "b47b0b1a-d99f-4bb5-9207-599e1d7ed483"

Text: "- `Equivalent:` members must use heading parameters directly, have one group
  kind, and agree on target shape, type/base facts, requirements, and
  capabilities.
- `Refines:` targets must agree with the base target. `implicitly:` must be only
  the inherited `specifies:` fact; `explicitly:` must add a property.
- Every `Justification:` entry must be referenced by a matching formulation
  label and restate its labeled `have:` formulation.
- Function type leaves use `_`; calls must match arity. Tuple forms and values
  have at least two elements.
- Inferred `X?` parameters introduce a name only once.
- Variadic ranges start at 0 or 1; paired broadcasts match exactly; 2D arguments
  are nonempty rectangles with equal row widths.
- `piecewise:` accepts repeated structural `elseIf:`/`then:` pairs and checks
  each branch under its condition."
Id: "9b7883ee-4c65-4c28-995a-c8d6fe0af139"
